# dist/ IS committed (see BACKLOG.md Story 1.7 / .claude/skills/release):
# this package isn't on npm yet, so a plain GitHub tarball URL install --
# the only option that doesn't need the `git` binary on the installing
# machine -- has no other way to get built output. Rebuilt + committed as
# part of every tagged release; may go slightly stale between releases on
# `develop`, which is fine since nobody installs from `develop`'s HEAD.
